From 918afd302e7ca345e771441c325452d40430198e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:18:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Phase 0 probe script for Productive's sub-task API

The extension cannot be written until we know whether a sub-task inherits the
parent's subscribers client-side (the web app pre-filling subscriber_ids) or
server-side. Those two answers need different create calls, and guessing wrong
sends notifications to client contacts.

scripts/phase0.mjs runs against a sandbox task and answers that empirically:

- read-only probes for the task shape, how subscribers are exposed, the correct
  subscribable_type, the people census that picks the staff signal, the workflow
  chain behind a "not started" status, and the project's watchers
- an eleven-row create matrix covering both JSON:API wire forms, since the docs
  describe flat subscriber_ids/assignee_id attributes while two independent
  public clients build the same fields as relationships
- a row that sends both forms with conflicting values, because a 201 alone does
  not reveal which form the server honored and which it dropped
- a control row with no parent, to establish the project's watcher floor
- a delayed re-read, which catches a server that adds subscribers a beat after
  the create returns

Read-only by default; creating needs --yes, and it refuses to arm when more than
three people besides the caller could be notified. Every created id is written to
a ledger before any follow-up read, and cleanup only ever deletes from that ledger.

Titles carry a unique token per row so the recipient can report which ones
actually generated mail. That report is the finding; the subscriber arrays the
API returns are not, since a clean array does not prove no notification fired.

